// 08 · Reef — space and structure: size-selective refugia.
//
// The physical/spatial levers composed into a REAL reef, where the rocks sort bodies BY
// SIZE. A solid source is a static circle collider (`Collider::circle(radius)`), so a
// disc of radius r threads a gap of width G (rock-surface to rock-surface) only when
// G ≥ 2·r. Ring six rocks around each of FOUR vents, leaving ~18 px gaps, and you get four
// **refuge gardens**:
//   • KELP (r 4, tiny anchored plants) grows on the sheltered vent inside each ring.
//   • the HERBIVORE (r 6, needs a 12 px gap) SLIPS THROUGH the gaps to graze it — and,
//     being a Hunter, flees a threat, sometimes ducking into a ring to escape.
//   • the OMNIVORE (r 12, needs a 24 px gap) is WALLED OUT — it eats kelp AND herbivores,
//     but the 18 px gaps block its body, so the ring interiors are refuges it cannot enter.
//     No behaviour rule draws the line; the geometry does (emergent, Law 8-ish for space):
//     the SAME rock is a wall to one body and a doorway to a smaller one.
//
// So the reef partitions the world by size: kelp and herbivores persist in the sheltered
// gardens the omnivore can only besiege from outside; a single OPEN vent in mid-water is the
// contested commons it is left with. The refuge is so effective that the excluded omnivore
// STARVES OUT — a size-structured reef that cannot support its would-be top predator (an
// example to watch early, ROADMAP §7). KELP is also ANCHORED (a spring): jostled it springs
// back, but a grazer's shove or a packed clump tears it loose past its tension → it uproots,
// dies, and drops DETRITUS (turnover, the mortality lever a standing crop needs; cf. 03).
//
// Watch (View ▸ Layers): kelp greens the four ring interiors and the open vent; small
// herbivores thread the gaps in and out; the big omnivore noses at the entrances but cannot
// follow, patrolling the open water. A Detritus patch blooms where kelp is torn loose. A
// lively example to watch, not a steady state (ROADMAP §7).
(
    tick_hz: 64.0,
    arena_half_extent: 380.0,
    archetypes: [
        (
            name: "Kelp",
            color: (0.30, 0.75, 0.50),
            count: 90,
            radius: 4.0,
            reserve_max: 50.0,
            genotype: (
                max_speed: 0.0,
                vision_range: 30.0,
                vision_rays: 1.0,
                reproduction_threshold: 22.0,
                offspring_energy: 13.0,
                mutation_rate: 0.0,
                photosynthesis: 6.5,
                seed_dispersal: 16.0,
            ),
            brain: Sessile,
            mutable: (
                max_speed: false,
                agility: false,
                vision_range: false,
                vision_fov: false,
                reproduction_threshold: false,
                offspring_energy: false,
                mutation_rate: false,
                vision_rays: false,
                photosynthesis: false,
                seed_dispersal: false,
                brain_cost: false,
                act_cost: false,
            ),
            // A spring roots each kelp to its seed point; jostling holds, but a grazer's
            // shove or a packed clump tears it loose past its tension → death → detritus.
            anchor: Some((stiffness: 30.0, damping: 3.0, tear_force: 700.0, die_on_detach: true)),
        ),
        (
            name: "Herbivore",
            color: (1.0, 0.72, 0.30),
            count: 12,
            radius: 6.0,
            reserve_max: 100.0,
            genotype: (
                max_speed: 115.0,
                agility: 0.14,
                vision_range: 120.0,
                vision_fov_deg: 130.0,
                reproduction_threshold: 90.0,
                offspring_energy: 38.0,
                mutation_rate: 0.06,
                vision_rays: 7.0,
            ),
            brain: Hunter,
            mutable: (mutation_rate: false),
        ),
        (
            name: "Omnivore",
            color: (0.95, 0.42, 0.38),
            count: 3,
            radius: 12.0,
            reserve_max: 220.0,
            genotype: (
                max_speed: 92.0,
                agility: 0.10,
                vision_range: 155.0,
                vision_fov_deg: 130.0,
                reproduction_threshold: 170.0,
                offspring_energy: 75.0,
                mutation_rate: 0.06,
                vision_rays: 7.0,
            ),
            brain: Hunter,
            mutable: (mutation_rate: false),
        ),
    ],
    // Metabolic cost bounds the kelp (Liebig): its photosynthesis draws down the nutrient,
    // so the reef holds a dense-but-bounded stand around the vents rather than carpeting.
    cost_law: (size_exponent: 2.0, maintenance: 0.04, locomotion: 0.02, maneuver: 0.0002, metabolic_cost: 0.25),
    // A tight eating reach: the omnivore must be right on its prey, so it cannot reach past
    // an 18 px gap to pick off a herbivore sheltering just inside the ring.
    predation: (size_margin: 0.1, range: 6.0, rate: 16.0),
    field_resolution: 256,
    components: [
        (name: "Nutrient", diffusion: 0.3, decay: 0.0),
        // Detritus lingers (low diffusion) and slowly fades — an uprooting leaves a visible,
        // localized patch that decomposes over time.
        (name: "Detritus", diffusion: 0.06, decay: 0.02),
    ],
    sources: [
